  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Visit of Dutch entrepreneurs to Sahara expo</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Sahara, the International Agricultural Exhibition for Africa and the Middle East, is the main platform for agriculture, animal production, and aquaculture in the MENA region.In the combi-track, a Dutch pavilion and trade mission to the Sahara expo on climate and water smart agriculture, was included in the activities.The Climate and Water Smart Agriculture (CaWSA) combi-track focusses on linking Egyptian, Dutch, and international companies, entrepreneurs and institutes, fostering trade, innovation, and entrepreneurship in the area of climate and water smart agriculture. This track works towards a resilient, future-proof farming system in Egypt, in which farmers, youth and women in particular, thrive.The goal of this project is to participate with a Dutch pavilion at Sahara with Dutch horticulture and agro-food companies and governmental/knowledge institutes.This will create the following opportunities:&#x2022;	Business opportunities between Dutch companies and Egyptian/MENA companies;- Knowledge exchange between Egyptian and Dutch companies on climate and water smart agriculture via a 3-day seminar programme.&#x2022;	Enhanced possibilities for further cooperation.&#x2022;	Promotion of selected Dutch funded programmes and activities in the agriculture sector in Egypt and identifications of new partnerships and activities between the Netherlands and Egypt (and the MENA region by extension) in the field of agri- and horticulture under the Dutch combi-track approach.&#x2022;	Positioning of the Netherlands, and its companies, as the partner in sustainable, innovative, climate-smart and circular agriculture and horticulture.</narrative>
  </description>
